# Cloudflare Pages equivalent of the firebase.json `headers` block.
#
# Rules are applied in order and later ones win for the same header, so the
# blanket immutable rule comes first and the entry points override it below.
#
# Caching everything for a year is safe *because* of those overrides: Flutter's
# service worker is the version check. It is fetched fresh, compares the asset
# hashes in its manifest, and re-fetches anything stale with `cache: 'reload'`.
# main.dart.js and the files under assets/ are not content-hashed, so if the
# service worker itself were cached, a deploy would never reach anyone.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/flutter_bootstrap.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/flutter_service_worker.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/version.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
